%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cedcb971d9918c84fb60186450419255, type: 3}
  m_Name: Module2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PhotoTextContentData
  data:
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Introduction
    description: 'In Information and Communication Technology (ICT), tools and equipment
      refer to the physical devices, hardware, and software used for various tasks
      related to processing, transmitting, storing, and managing information. These
      tools and equipment play a crucial role in enabling individuals and organizations
      to work efficiently and effectively in the digital age. Here are some examples
      of tools and equipment in ICT:

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Hardware

'
    description: Hardware refers to physical electronic components and devices used
      in computing and technology systems. These physical components include items
      such as circuit boards, processors, memory modules, storage devices (like hard
      drives and solid-state drives), input and output devices (such as keyboards,
      mice, monitors, and printers), and various other peripherals like graphics
      cards and network adapters. Hardware is essential for the operation and functionality
      of computers, servers, smartphones, and other electronic devices.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Computer
    description: 'A computer is the most fundamental tool for programming. It can
      be a desktop, laptop, or even a cloud-based virtual machine, depending on the
      requirements of the project.

      

      Desktop Computer: A desktop computer
      is a type of personal computer designed to be used on a desk or work surface.
      It typically consists of several components, including a central processing
      unit (CPU), Motherboard, HDD/SDD, Memory, PSU, monitor, keyboard, mouse, and
      various peripherals. Desktop computers are known for their power, expandability,
      and the ability to perform a wide range of tasks, including gaming, content
      creation, software development, and office work. They are not portable and
      are meant to stay in one location.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Keyboard and Mouse
    description: 'A comfortable keyboard and mouse are essential for efficient typing
      and navigation while writing code.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Monitor
    description: ' A good quality monitor with a high resolution provides programmers
      with more screen real estate for coding, debugging, and testing.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Printer
    description: 'is a peripheral device commonly used with computers and other digital
      devices to produce physical copies of digital documents, images, or graphics
      on paper or other printable materials.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Scanner
    description: 'is a digital input device that is used to convert physical documents,
      images, or objects into digital format, which can then be stored, manipulated,
      and displayed on a computer or other digital devices.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Webcam
    description: 'is short for "web camera," is a digital camera device typically
      built into or connected to a computer, laptop, or other digital devices. Webcams
      are designed for capturing live video and audio and transmitting it in real-time
      over the internet.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Light Pen
    description: ' is a handheld input device that was used in the early days of
      computing and graphical user interfaces (GUIs) to interact with a computer''s
      display screen.'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Digitize Tablet
    description: 'also known as a graphics tablet, pen tablet, or drawing tablet,
      is a specialized input device used by artists, graphic designers, and professionals
      in creative fields for creating digital illustrations, graphics, and designs.
      It consists of a flat, rectangular surface (the tablet) and a stylus or pen-like
      input device.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Speaker '
    description: 'These speakers are specifically engineered to provide sound output
      for various multimedia applications, including music, videos, games, and more.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'AVR '
    description: "stands for Automatic Voltage Regulator. It refers to a device or
      system that automatically adjusts the voltage output of a generator or electrical
      source to maintain a stable and consistent voltage level. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Headset '
    description: 'is a combination of headphones (or earphones) and a microphone,
      typically integrated into a single device or connected as separate components.
      Headsets are designed for audio communication, allowing users to both listen
      to audio and speak into the microphone simultaneously.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'UPS '
    description: " stands for Uninterruptible Power Supply. It is a device used to
      provide backup power to electrical devices or systems in the event of a power
      outage or disruption. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Laptop, short for "notebook computer
    description: 'is a portable personal computer designed for mobility and convenience.
      Unlike traditional desktop computers that remain stationary on a desk, a laptop
      is compact and lightweight, allowing users to carry it with them and use it
      virtually anywhere.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Minicomputer '
    description: ' it is referred to as a server, utilized by small to medium-sized
      enterprises, and typically accommodates the needs of hundreds of users.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Mainframe Computer
    description: "is a sizable and costly computing system with the capability to
      accommodate hundreds or even thousands of users. \r\n\r\n\r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Supercomputer
    description: ' is the fastest category of computer designed for specific applications,
      capable of handling massive volumes of data processing. '
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Storage Device
    description: A storage device is a hardware component or device that is used
      to store, save, and retain digital data or information. These devices are essential
      for preserving and accessing data over extended periods.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Hard Disk Drive (HDD)
    description: " are mechanical storage devices that use spinning platters to store
      data. They are commonly found in desktop and laptop computers, as well as external
      drives. HDDs offer high capacity but are relatively slower than some newer
      storage technologies. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Solid-State Drive (SSD) '
    description: ' are a type of storage device that uses NAND flash memory to store
      data. They are faster and more durable than HDDs and are commonly used in laptops,
      desktops, and high-performance computing systems.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'USB Flash Drive '
    description: Also known as thumb drives or USB sticks, these small, portable
      devices use flash memory to store data. USB drives are highly portable and
      can be plugged into USB ports on computers and other devices.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: External Hard Drive
    description: 'These are standalone HDD or SSD storage devices enclosed in an
      external casing. They connect to computers via USB, Thunderbolt, or other interfaces
      and are often used for data backup and expansion.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Network Attached Storage (NAS)
    description: 'devices are specialized storage devices that are connected to a
      network, allowing multiple users to access and share data. They are commonly
      used in homes and small businesses for centralized data storage and backup.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Cloud Storage
    description: ' services allow users to store their data on remote servers accessible
      over the internet. Popular cloud storage providers include Dropbox, Google
      Drive, and Microsoft OneDrive.'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Memory Cards
    description: ' such as SD cards and microSD cards, are used in digital cameras,
      smartphones, and other portable devices to store photos, videos, and other
      data.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Network Device
    description: ' A network device is a hardware component or equipment used in
      computer networks to facilitate communication, data transfer, and the management
      of network resources. These devices play essential roles in enabling devices
      within a network to connect, communicate, and share data efficiently.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Modem '
    description: 'A modem (short for modulator-demodulator) is a device that modulates
      digital data from a computer into analog signals for transmission over telephone
      lines (DSL modem) or cable lines (cable modem) and demodulates incoming analog
      signals back into digital data.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Router '
    description: 'are key network devices that connect different networks together,
      such as a local network to the internet. They determine the best path for data
      packets to travel between networks, manage IP addresses, and provide security
      features like firewalls.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Switch '
    description: 'A network switch is used to connect devices within the same local
      area network (LAN). It operates at Layer 2 (Data Link Layer) of the OSI model
      and is responsible for forwarding data frames to the appropriate device based
      on MAC (Media Access Control) addresses.


      Unmanage Switch - An "unmanaged
      switch" is a type of network switch that operates without the ability for remote
      configuration and management by a network administrator.

      

      

      

      

      Manage
      Switch - A managed switch is a type of network switch that offers advanced
      features and can be configured and controlled by network administrators.

      

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Hub '
    description: are older network devices that operate at the physical layer (Layer
      1) of the OSI model. They broadcast data to all devices connected to them,
      making them less efficient than switches, which selectively forward data.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Access Point (AP)
    description: 'are used to provide wireless connectivity to devices in a Wi-Fi
      network. They allow wireless devices like laptops and smartphones to connect
      to a wired network.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Firewall '
    description: "are network security devices that filter and control incoming and
      outgoing network traffic based on predefined security rules. They protect networks
      from unauthorized access and threats. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Network Interface Card (NIC)
    description: "are hardware components installed in computers and devices to enable
      them to connect to a network. They provide the physical connection to the network
      medium, such as Ethernet or Wi-Fi. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Server Cabinet
    description: 'also known as a network cabinet, server rack, or data cabinet,
      is a specialized enclosure designed to house and protect various networking
      and server equipment within a data center or server room. These cabinets provide
      a secure and organized environment for servers, networking devices, and other
      IT equipment.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Patch Panel
    description: " is a network hardware device that serves as a central point for
      the organization and management of network cables. It allows network administrators
      to easily connect, disconnect, and rearrange the various network cables within
      a data center or network closet. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Cable Manager
    description: "also known as a cable management system or cable management panel,
      is an essential component in a server cabinet or network rack that is used
      to organize and manage network and power cables within the cabinet. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Patch Cable
    description: is a short, standardized cable with connectors on both ends used
      to establish a temporary or permanent connection between network devices, such
      as computers, switches, routers, and patch panels.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Electronic Tester VOM (Voltage-Ohm-Milliammeter) '
    description: 'VOM is a versatile handheld device used to measure electrical properties
      in circuits and components. It typically measures voltage (in volts), resistance
      (in ohms), and current (in milliamperes or amps).

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: LAN Cable Tester
    description: " A LAN (Local Area Network) cable tester is a specialized tool
      used to test and troubleshoot Ethernet and networking cables, such as Cat 5e,
      Cat 6, or Cat 7 cables. It helps verify cable continuity, pin configurations,
      and detects wiring faults, ensuring that network connections are properly established
      and free from issues. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Other Tools and Equipment
    description: 'The following tools and equipment are specifically used in the
      Computer System Servicing field of ICT.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Screwdriver Standard
    description: A screwdriver with a flat, blade-like tip used for turning screws
      with a single, straight-line groove or slot.
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Screwdriver Philips
    description: 'A screwdriver with a cross-shaped tip used for turning screws with
      a cross-shaped or Phillips head.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Long Nose Plier
    description: 'Pliers with elongated, pointed jaws used for gripping, bending,
      and manipulating small objects or wires in tight spaces.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Mechanical Plier
    description: ' Pliers designed for mechanical work, such as bending, crimping,
      or cutting wires and other materials.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Wire Cutter
    description: ' A tool designed to cut wires and cables cleanly and efficiently.

      

      

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Allen Wrench
    description: 'Also known as a hex key or hex wrench, it''s a tool with a hexagonal-shaped
      tip used to turn bolts and screws with hexagonal sockets.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Part Retriever
    description: "A tool designed to retrieve small parts or objects from tight or
      hard-to-reach places. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Crimping Tools
    description: 'Tools used for crimping, or compressing, connectors onto the ends
      of cables or wires to create secure electrical connections.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Anti-Static Mat
    description: ' is a specialized mat designed to prevent the buildup and discharge
      of static electricity, particularly in environments where sensitive electronic
      components, devices, or equipment are handled or assembled.'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Anti-Static Wrist
    description: ' A wristband with an attached cord that helps to dissipate static
      electricity from a person''s body to prevent electrostatic discharge (ESD)
      when working with sensitive electronic equipment.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Wire Stripper
    description: "A tool designed to remove the insulation or outer sheath from electrical
      wires, exposing the conductor for connections. \r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Precision Screwdrivers
    description: ' Screwdrivers with very small and precise tips, often used for
      delicate tasks like working with small electronic components or intricate mechanisms.'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Flashlight
    description: 'It is commonly used in various fields, including electronics, to
      provide additional illumination in low-light or confined spaces when working
      on tasks that require precision and visibility.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Fiber optic (terminated)
    description: 'Fiber optic cables transmit data using light signals and require
      precise terminations for optimal performance. Terminated fiber optic cables
      are ready for use and can be connected to networking equipment, such as switches
      or transceivers, to establish high-speed data connections over long distances
      with minimal signal loss.

'
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Ergonomic Computer Tables and Chairs
    description: ' Ergonomic computer tables and chairs are specially designed furniture
      pieces that prioritize comfort, efficiency, and well-being for individuals
      who spend extended periods working or using a computer. These ergonomic furnishings
      are essential in promoting proper posture, reducing strain, and enhancing overall
      productivity.

'
    has3dView: 0
